* r70_stream_binding.dts
* AIF-120 R70 -- the stream side of the generated grid binding, measured.
*
* The generated wx grid declares its columns from BINDING (contract 10c) and then
* fills them from DbTupleStream. This proves the two halves AGREE: the columns the
* generator writes into InsertColumn are exactly the values the engine returns for
* the same spec, in the same order. A generator whose heads and rows disagree
* compiles perfectly and renders a lie.
*
* Fixture: STUDENTS + ENROLL from the shipped x64 school tables, related on SID --
* the FRAMEDEMO document's own SOURCE. Read-only throughout.
*
* Regression doctrine: every test sets its own environment.

SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF
SET PATH DBF dbf/x64

FORMULA "AIF120-R70-STREAM-BEGIN"

ECHO
ECHO --- FRAMEDEMO SOURCE: two aliases, one Relation edge ---
SELECT 1
USE STUDENTS
SELECT 2
USE ENROLL
SELECT 1
SET RELATION TO SID INTO ENROLL

ECHO
ECHO --- A. the spec resolves to FOUR values, one per generated column ---
ECHO A1 heads the generator emits: LNAME FNAME CLS_ID GRADE
GOTO FIRST
ECHO A2 the engine returns:
TUPLE students.lname,students.fname,enroll.cls_id,enroll.grade

ECHO
ECHO --- B. next_page(3) is three DISTINCT rows, not one row three times ---
ECHO B1 row 1
TUPLE students.lname,students.fname,enroll.cls_id,enroll.grade
SKIP
ECHO B2 row 2
TUPLE students.lname,students.fname,enroll.cls_id,enroll.grade
SKIP
ECHO B3 row 3
TUPLE students.lname,students.fname,enroll.cls_id,enroll.grade

ECHO
ECHO --- C. a one-alias spec is the P2/P6 case ---
GOTO FIRST
TUPLE students.lname,students.fname

ECHO
ECHO --- D. alias.* is the N9/N10 case: the whole record, one alias ---
TUPLE students.*

ECHO
ECHO --- E. R65.3 again, from HELP's OWN documented syntax ---
ECHO E1 HELP TUPLE documents "TUPLE #11.*"; the AIF-037 lexer cuts # to end of line
TUPLE #1.lname
ECHO E2 ...which is why contract 10c REFUSES an ordinal spec instead of emitting it

WORKSPACE CLOSE

FORMULA "AIF120-R70-STREAM-END"
